      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.45,
          "en": "Instructor: So, how can you migrate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.45,
          "end": 5.73,
          "en": "those components to standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.73,
          "end": 7.98,
          "en": "and which adjustments are needed, then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.98,
          "end": 10.62,
          "en": "Let's start with the about component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.62,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "Here, we can add the standalone flag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 15.78,
          "en": "just as we did it before, and set it to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.78,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "And if this component would be using any other directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 21.18,
          "en": "or other standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.18,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "we would have to add them here, to the imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 27.57,
          "en": "But for this component, that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.57,
          "end": 30.45,
          "en": "And now, this about component is, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.45,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "referenced here in app routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "There we have this about component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "at which we're pointing, which we wanna load here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 42.12,
          "en": "Now, if we are dealing with a standalone component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.12,
          "end": 43.65,
          "en": "this will still work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.65,
          "end": 46.89,
          "en": "If I save this code, if I even restart NG serve,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.89,
          "end": 49.62,
          "en": "to be super safe, that this all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.62,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "You will notice that if I reload the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 54.21,
          "en": "we can still visit about, as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.21,
          "end": 57.42,
          "en": "So, you can use standalone components here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.42,
          "end": 59.58,
          "en": "And this shouldn't be too surprising",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.58,
          "end": 61.08,
          "en": "because the welcome component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.08,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "already was a standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 66.81,
          "en": "and navigating to it worked just fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.81,
          "end": 69.938,
          "en": "However, if you are dealing with standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.938,
          "end": 72.96000000000001,
          "en": "you can also load them with a different syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.96000000000001,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "which will actually use lazy loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 78.15,
          "en": "Because with this syntax here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.15,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "you are not loading this component lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.42,
          "en": "Instead, it is included in the main bundle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.42,
          "end": 86.49,
          "en": "But with a standalone component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 90.27,
          "en": "you can go to your route configuration here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.27,
          "end": 94.083,
          "en": "and add a special load component key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.13,
          "end": 98.52000000000001,
          "en": "And now load component, just like load children,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "takes a function which should return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "the result of calling import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 106.65,
          "en": "And then here, we point at the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.65,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "which we wanna load lazily, add then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 113.43,
          "en": "and then simply extract our component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.43,
          "end": 115.62,
          "en": "from the module which is loaded lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.62,
          "end": 118.413,
          "en": "So, from the file, which is loaded lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 123.24,
          "en": "Now, this is a brand new feature, a brand new syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.24,
          "end": 126.96,
          "en": "which only works with standalone components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.96,
          "end": 130.62,
          "en": "If we save this, the application works like before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.62,
          "end": 132.72,
          "en": "We can still go to the about page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.72,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "but if you open the network tab again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 136.95,
          "en": "and you reload the app on the homepage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.95,
          "end": 139.07999999999998,
          "en": "you will note that when you go to about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.07999999999998,
          "end": 140.31,
          "en": "the code for this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.31,
          "end": 143.31,
          "en": "is all just downloaded when it's needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.31,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "And this is actually an enhancement you get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.74,
          "end": 147.72,
          "en": "with standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 150.51,
          "en": "because now with standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 153.96,
          "en": "you can load individual components lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.96,
          "end": 156.93,
          "en": "without having to wrap them into a module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 156.93,
          "end": 161.34,
          "en": "like this dashboard routing module, which uses for child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.34,
          "end": 163.44,
          "en": "Without standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 163.44,
          "end": 167.22,
          "en": "even if you just wanna load a single component lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "you, basically, have to wrap it into such a routing module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 173.94,
          "en": "where you use router module for child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 173.94,
          "end": 177.69,
          "en": "and then you have to load that router module lazily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.69,
          "end": 179.1,
          "en": "with load children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 179.1,
          "end": 182.19,
          "en": "That's how you have to do it prior to version 14,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 182.19,
          "end": 184.62,
          "en": "without standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 184.62,
          "end": 187.923,
          "en": "even if it's just one component you wanna load lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 191.04,
          "en": "Here with standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.04,
          "end": 193.02,
          "en": "this is now made way simpler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.02,
          "end": 195.99,
          "en": "We can use load component and point directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.99,
          "end": 198.66,
          "en": "at the component which we wanna load lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 201.78,
          "en": "You don't need an extra wrapper routing module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 205.023,
          "en": "So, this is a great simplification which we get here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 206.1,
          "end": 208.53,
          "en": "Now, if you have multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 208.53,
          "end": 210.21,
          "en": "that should be loaded lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 210.21,
          "end": 212.28,
          "en": "you can still use the old approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 212.28,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "of having a separate wrapper module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 217.53,
          "en": "but it's also not something you have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 217.53,
          "end": 220.38,
          "en": "You can simplify this code, as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.38,
          "end": 221.97,
          "en": "And for this, first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 221.97,
          "end": 225.96,
          "en": "let's turn these components, today and dashboard component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 225.96,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "into standalone components as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 231.123,
          "en": "by adding the standalone true flag to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 232.17000000000002,
          "end": 234.21,
          "en": "Now, these are standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 234.21,
          "end": 237,
          "en": "and we could use them in any of our components",
