        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 237,
          "end": 240.63,
          "en": "by adding them to the imports array of those components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 240.63,
          "end": 242.78,
          "en": "But, we can also use them with the routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 243.69,
          "end": 246.57,
          "en": "Of course, back in our app routing module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 246.57,
          "end": 251.43,
          "en": "we could use them by simply repeating this syntax here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 251.43,
          "end": 252.63,
          "en": "for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 252.63,
          "end": 255.873,
          "en": "or even without lazy loading with this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 256.83,
          "end": 259.95,
          "en": "But we can also still use load children,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 259.95,
          "end": 263.46,
          "en": "but instead of adding this extra wrapper module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 263.46,
          "end": 265.44,
          "en": "and this extra module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 265.44,
          "end": 268.74,
          "en": "we can get rid of dashboard module TS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 268.74,
          "end": 273.54,
          "en": "and actually also get rid of dashboard routing module TS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 273.54,
          "end": 275.97,
          "en": "And instead here, in the dashboard folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 275.97,
          "end": 279.18,
          "en": "which has these components which I wanna load via routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 279.18,
          "end": 282.65999999999997,
          "en": "we can add a new file, for example, named routes TS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 282.65999999999997,
          "end": 284.73,
          "en": "The name is up to you though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 284.73,
          "end": 287.07,
          "en": "And in that file, you can simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 287.07,
          "end": 289.5,
          "en": "export a constant or a variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 289.5,
          "end": 291.93,
          "en": "maybe named dashboard routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 291.93,
          "end": 293.073,
          "en": "The name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 294.15,
          "end": 297.003,
          "en": "And that should be of type route array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 298.05,
          "end": 300.963,
          "en": "Route is a type imported from Angular router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 301.8,
          "end": 305.49,
          "en": "And then here, you set up your route configuration objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 305.49,
          "end": 308.28,
          "en": "and you have a path, nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 308.28,
          "end": 312.18,
          "en": "which should maybe load the dashboard component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 312.18,
          "end": 314.43,
          "en": "So, you must import this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 314.43,
          "end": 316.173,
          "en": "and then point at it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 317.25,
          "end": 322.11,
          "en": "And you add a never object, with a path of today,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 322.11,
          "end": 325.14300000000003,
          "en": "where you point at the today component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 326.19,
          "end": 329.31,
          "en": "Alternatively here, you could also use load component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 329.31,
          "end": 333.03,
          "en": "to load this component lazily, only if it's needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.03,
          "end": 336.6,
          "en": "So, you could be more granular if you wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 336.6,
          "end": 338.88,
          "en": "Here, I'm loading both routes together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 338.88,
          "end": 341.43,
          "en": "but not when the application starts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.43,
          "end": 342.93,
          "en": "but instead when we navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 342.93,
          "end": 346.05,
          "en": "to the dashboard area of this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 346.05,
          "end": 348.96,
          "en": "And here, we just have a route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 348.96,
          "end": 351.65999999999997,
          "en": "To make Angular aware of this, what we can do now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 351.65999999999997,
          "end": 353.37,
          "en": "and what we have to do now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 353.37,
          "end": 356.58,
          "en": "is we have to go back to the app routing module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 356.58,
          "end": 358.83,
          "en": "And here, for the dashboard route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 358.83,
          "end": 360.48,
          "en": "instead of using load children",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 360.48,
          "end": 363.69,
          "en": "to point at the dashboard routing module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 363.69,
          "end": 368.04,
          "en": "we use it to point at dashboard slash routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 368.04,
          "end": 369.69,
          "en": "And then from that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 369.69,
          "end": 372.63,
          "en": "we import the dashboard routes constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 372.63,
          "end": 373.773,
          "en": "which we exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 374.94,
          "end": 378.21,
          "en": "So, this will now load these routes lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 378.21,
          "end": 382.68,
          "en": "but we only need to define the route definitions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 382.68,
          "end": 384.9,
          "en": "So again, we save a lot of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 384.9,
          "end": 387.03,
          "en": "We don't need the wrapper modules",
          "zh": ""
